Objective: Verify default reset values and masked read/write behavior for a set of GPIO GP0 registers using array-driven sequences.
Initialization: Global counters def_fail_cnt=0 and wr_fail_cnt=0. Arrays defined: addr_array[20], default_value_array[20], read_mask_array[20], write_mask_array[20], skip_array[20], skip_rst_array[20].
Flow:
- test_case():
  - Calls chk_rst_val();
  - Calls chk_rd_wr();
  - If (def_fail_cnt > 0 || wr_fail_cnt > 0) finish(1); else finish(0).
- chk_rst_val():
  - For (i = 0; i < CNT; i++):
    - addr = addr_array[i];
    - If (skip_rst_array[i] == 1) continue;
    - If (read_mask_array[i] == 0x00000000) continue;
    - data_rd = read_reg(addr);
    - data = (data_rd & 0xfffffffe);
    - If (data == default_value_array[i]) PASS; else { def_fail_cnt++; printf failure message with addr, expected, read, raw }.
